  {
    "ref": "Misc I Q.19",
    "bucket": "exercise-mcq",
    "format": "mcq",
    "subtopic": "Trigonometric Equations and General Solutions",
    "difficulty": "HARD",
    "stem": "If \\(\\tan\\theta + \\tan 2\\theta + \\tan 3\\theta = \\tan\\theta\\,\\tan 2\\theta\\,\\tan 3\\theta\\), then the general value of \\(\\theta\\) is ______.",
    "options": [
      {"label": "A", "text": "\\(n\\pi\\)"},
      {"label": "B", "text": "\\(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{6}\\)"},
      {"label": "C", "text": "\\(n\\pi \\pm \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\)"},
      {"label": "D", "text": "\\(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}\\)"}
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "solution": "[Textbook defect: the complete solution set is \\(\\theta=\\dfrac{n\\pi}{3}\\), which is not among the four printed alternatives. The official key marks \\(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{6}\\), retained here to match the board: it contains the whole solution set as its even-\\(n\\) members, but also contains values such as \\(\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\) at which \\(\\tan 3\\theta\\) is undefined.]\n\nSince \\(3\\theta=\\theta+2\\theta\\), \\(\\tan 3\\theta=\\dfrac{\\tan\\theta+\\tan 2\\theta}{1-\\tan\\theta\\tan 2\\theta}\\), that is \\(\\tan\\theta+\\tan 2\\theta=\\tan 3\\theta\\left(1-\\tan\\theta\\tan 2\\theta\\right)\\).\n\nSubstituting this in the given equation:\n\n\\(\\tan 3\\theta\\left(1-\\tan\\theta\\tan 2\\theta\\right)+\\tan 3\\theta=\\tan\\theta\\tan 2\\theta\\tan 3\\theta\\)\n\n\\(\\Rightarrow\\ 2\\tan 3\\theta\\left(1-\\tan\\theta\\tan 2\\theta\\right)=0\\).\n\nThe factor \\(1-\\tan\\theta\\tan 2\\theta\\) vanishes exactly where \\(\\tan 3\\theta\\) is undefined, so it yields no solution of the given equation. Hence \\(\\tan 3\\theta=0\\), i.e. \\(3\\theta=n\\pi\\), giving \\(\\theta=\\dfrac{n\\pi}{3}\\).\n\nFollowing the official key, (B)."
  },
  {
    "ref": "Misc I Q.20",
    "bucket": "exercise-mcq",
    "format": "mcq",
    "subtopic": "Applications of Sine, Cosine and Projection Rules",
    "difficulty": "MODERATE",
    "stem": "In any \\(\\triangle ABC\\), if \\(a\\cos B = b\\cos A\\), then the triangle is ______.",
    "options": [
      {"label": "A", "text": "Equilateral triangle"},
      {"label": "B", "text": "Isosceles triangle"},
      {"label": "C", "text": "Scalene"},
      {"label": "D", "text": "Right angled"}
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "solution": "By sine rule \\(a\\cos B=b\\cos A\\Rightarrow\\sin A\\cos B=\\sin B\\cos A\\Rightarrow\\sin(A-B)=0\\Rightarrow A=B\\); the triangle is isosceles."
  },

